  solution        : "First ensure that systemd is correctly configured to ensure that /tmp will be mounted at boot time. # systemctl unmask tmp.mount For specific configuration requirements of the /tmp mount for your environment, modify /etc/fstab. Example of using tmpfs with specific mount options: tmpfs /tmp tmpfs defaults,rw,nosuid,nodev,noexec,relatime,size=2G 0 0"
  reference       : "NIST 800-53r5|AC-3 AC-5 AC-6 CM-6b. MP-2"
  see_also        : "See HTH Policies and Standards"
  show_output     : "YES"
</report>
      </then>
